{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}{{ m.bot_label.split(' (')[0] }} · CHAKRAVYUH scorecard{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
{% set bot_name = m.bot_label.split(' (')[0] %}
{% set ci_lo = ((s.call_pass_ci95[0] or 0) * 100)|round(1) %}{% set ci_hi = ((s.call_pass_ci95[1] or 0) * 100)|round(1) %}
{% set rate = ((s.calls_passed / s.calls * 100) if s.calls else 0)|round(1) %}

<div class="eyebrow"><span>Scorecard</span><span class="dot"></span><span class="mono">{{ m.run_id }}</span><span class="dot"></span><span>{{ 'Offline dry run' if offline else 'Live run' }}</span></div>
<h1>{{ bot_name }}</h1>
<p class="lead">{{ s.calls }} synthetic call{{ '' if s.calls == 1 else 's' }} over simulated Indian phone lines, each one judged turn by turn. Every failure below comes with the exact quote and the audio as it sounded through the line.</p>
<div class="specs">
  <span class="spec"><span>Bot brain</span><b>{{ m.models.bot or m.bot_label }}</b></span>
  <span class="spec"><span>Callers</span><b>{{ m.models.persona }}</b></span>
  <span class="spec"><span>Ears</span><b>Gnani {{ m.models.stt }}</b></span>
  <span class="spec"><span>Voices</span><b>Gnani {{ m.models.tts }}</b></span>
  <span class="spec"><span>Judge</span><b>{{ s.judge_model }}</b></span>
  <span class="spec"><span>Mode</span><b>turn-based · barge-in N/A</b></span>
</div>

<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi hero">
    <div class="lbl">{{ ICON.grid|safe }}Scenarios passed</div>
    <div class="val num">{{ s.cells_passed }}<small> / {{ s.cells_total }}</small></div>
    <div class="foot">A scenario passes when ≥ 2 of 3 seeds pass</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="lbl">{{ ICON.phone|safe }}Calls passed</div>
    <div class="val num">{{ s.calls_passed }}<small> / {{ s.calls }}</small></div>
    <div class="ci" title="95% Wilson confidence interval"><div class="ci-band" style="left:{{ ci_lo }}%;width:{{ [ci_hi - ci_lo, 1]|max }}%"></div><div class="ci-dot" style="left:{{ rate }}%"></div></div>
    <div class="foot">95% CI {{ s.call_pass_ci95[0]|pct }} – {{ s.call_pass_ci95[1]|pct }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi {{ 'danger' if leaks else 'good' }}">
    <div class="lbl">{{ ICON.shield|safe }}Leaked an identifier</div>
    <div class="val num">{{ leaks }}<small> call{{ '' if leaks == 1 else 's' }}</small></div>
    <div class="foot">Fake account, mobile, PAN or OTP spoken aloud</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="lbl">{{ ICON.clock|safe }}Time to first word</div>
    <div class="val num">{{ s.latency_to_first_word_s.p50 if s.latency_to_first_word_s.p50 is not none else '–' }}<small>s p50</small></div>
    <div class="foot">p90 {{ s.latency_to_first_word_s.p90 if s.latency_to_first_word_s.p90 is not none else '–' }}s · fails above 3 s</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi">
    <div class="lbl">{{ ICON.wave|safe }}Line-noise errors</div>
    <div class="val num">{{ s.failure_kinds.harness }}</div>
    <div class="foot">Failures caused by the phone line, not the bot</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="sec"><span class="k">01</span><h2>Callers × scenarios</h2><p>Each tile is one caller trying one task, across seeds. Red tiles list what went wrong.</p></div>
<div class="card scroll"><table class="matrix">
<tr><th></th>{% for sc in scenarios %}<th>{{ sc|nice }}</th>{% endfor %}</tr>
{% for p in personas %}<tr><td class="who">{{ p|nice }}<small>{{ p }}</small></td>
{% for sc in scenarios %}{% set c = grid.get((p, sc)) %}<td>
  {% if c %}<div class="tile {{ 'pass' if c.cell_pass else 'fail' }}">
    <div class="t-top"><span class="badge {{ 'pass' if c.cell_pass else 'fail' }}">{{ 'Pass' if c.cell_pass else 'Fail' }}</span><span class="t-seeds">{{ c.passed_seeds }}/{{ c.seeds }} seeds</span></div>
    {% if c.failing_criteria %}<div class="t-chips">{% for k, n in c.failing_criteria.items() %}<span class="chip f">{{ CRIT.get(k, k) }}{% if n > 1 %} ×{{ n }}{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>{% else %}<div class="tile na">not run</div>{% endif %}
</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>

<div class="sec"><span class="k">02</span><h2>Hear it fail</h2><p>{{ failures|length }} failing call{{ '' if failures|length == 1 else 's' }}. Rule-based checks can't be overruled; the LLM judge must quote the transcript, and every quote is machine-verified.</p></div>
{% for r in failures %}{% set kind = r.v.failure_kind %}
<article class="fcard">
  <header class="fhead">
    <span class="badge {{ 'fail' if kind == 'bot' else 'warn' }}">{{ 'Bot failure' if kind == 'bot' else ('Line noise' if kind == 'harness' else 'Needs review') }}</span>
    <h3>{{ r.v.persona_id|nice }}<span class="arr">→</span>{{ r.v.scenario_id|nice }}</h3>
    <div class="fmeta"><span class="chip">{{ ICON.phone|safe }}{{ r.call.channel|nice }}</span><span class="chip">seed {{ r.v.seed }}</span><span class="chip">{{ r.call.turns|length - 1 }} turns</span></div>
  </header>
  <div class="fbody">
    <div class="checks">{% set ns = namespace(seen=[]) %}
    {% for c in r.failed %}
      <div class="check">
        <div class="check-top"><span class="x {{ 'u' if c.status == 'unverified' else '' }}">{{ (ICON.alert if c.status == 'unverified' else ICON.x)|safe }}</span><b>{{ CRIT.get(c.name, c.name) }}</b>
          {% if c.source == 'deterministic' %}<span class="src">rule check</span>{% elif c.status == 'unverified' %}<span class="src">unverified</span>{% else %}<span class="src">{{ ICON.check|safe }}LLM judge · quote verified</span>{% endif %}</div>
        <p class="reason">{{ c.reason }}</p>
        {% for e in c.evidence[:1] %}{% set key = e.turn|string ~ (e.quote or '')[:60] %}
          {% if key in ns.seen %}<div class="same">↑ same evidence as above · turn {{ e.turn }}</div>
          {% else %}{% set ns.seen = ns.seen + [key] %}<figure class="quote"><figcaption>Bot said · turn {{ e.turn }}</figcaption><blockquote>{{ e.quote }}</blockquote>{% if e.detail %}<div class="qd">{{ e.detail }}</div>{% endif %}</figure>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <aside class="listen">
      <div class="listen-h">{{ ICON.head|safe }}Listen through the line</div>
      {% for t in r.evidence_turns %}
      <div class="track"><div class="tl">Turn {{ t.index }}<span>{{ r.call.channel }}</span></div>
        {% if t.audio.caller_line %}<div class="row"><span>Caller → bot</span><audio controls preload="none" src="{{ r.prefix }}{{ t.audio.caller_line }}"></audio></div>{% endif %}
        {% if t.audio.bot_line %}<div class="row"><span>Bot → caller</span><audio controls preload="none" src="{{ r.prefix }}{{ t.audio.bot_line }}"></audio></div>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {% else %}<p class="muted" style="font-size:13px">No audio evidence for this call.</p>{% endfor %}
    </aside>
  </div>
  <details class="tx"><summary>{{ ICON.chev|safe }}Full transcript · {{ r.call.turns|length }} turns</summary>
  <div class="chat">
  {% for t in r.call.turns %}
    {% if t.caller_text %}<div class="msg caller"><div class="who"><span>Caller · turn {{ t.index }}</span></div>{{ t.caller_text }}
      {% if t.bot_heard_caller is not none %}<div class="heard">Bot heard: {{ t.bot_heard_caller }}</div>{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}
    <div class="msg bot"><div class="who"><span>Bot · {{ 'greeting' if t.index == 0 else 'turn ' ~ t.index }}</span></div>{{ t.bot_text_true or t.bot_text_heard }}
      {% if t.bot_text_true and t.bot_text_heard != t.bot_text_true %}<div class="heard">Caller heard: {{ t.bot_text_heard }}</div>{% endif %}
      <div class="meta">first word {{ '%.1f'|format((t.timing.response_latency_s or 0) + (t.timing.leading_silence_s or 0)) }}s · max gap {{ t.timing.max_internal_gap_s or 0 }}s{% if t.channel_meta.upstream %} · line loss {{ (t.channel_meta.upstream.measured_loss * 100)|round(1) }}%{% endif %}</div></div>
  {% endfor %}
  </div></details>
</article>
{% else %}
<div class="card pad"><span class="badge pass">All clear</span> <span class="muted">No failing calls in this run.</span></div>
{% endfor %}

<div class="sec"><span class="k">03</span><h2>Phone-line noise floor</h2><p>How much Gnani Prisma mishears the bot through each simulated line. Phonetic CER maps every script to Latin and numbers to digits, so "बैलेंस" = "balance". It measures mishearing, not spelling. A failure that vanishes on the bot's real text is blamed on the line, not the bot.</p></div>
<div class="card scroll"><table class="tbl">
<tr><th>Line</th><th>What it simulates</th><th>Phonetic CER</th><th></th><th>Median</th><th>Raw CER</th><th>Bot turns</th></tr>
{% for name, n in s.harness_noise_cer.items() %}<tr>
  <td><b>{{ name|nice }}</b><div class="mono muted">{{ name }}</div></td>
  <td class="muted" style="max-width:340px">{{ profiles[name].description if name in profiles else '' }}</td>
  <td class="mono num"><b>{{ n.mean|pct }}</b></td>
  <td style="width:22%"><div class="bar {{ 'f' if (n.mean or 0) > 0.25 else '' }}"><i style="width:{{ [((n.mean or 0) * 100)|round(1), 100]|min }}%"></i></div></td>
  <td class="mono num">{{ n.median|pct }}</td><td class="mono num muted">{{ n.raw_mean|pct }}</td><td class="mono num">{{ n.turns }}</td>
</tr>{% endfor %}
</table></div>

<div class="sec"><span class="k">04</span><h2>How the judge works</h2></div>
<div class="method">
  <div class="mitem"><b>{{ ICON.shield|safe }}Rules first</b><p>PII canaries, language, dead air and repetition are checked in code before any LLM looks at the call. The LLM can't overrule them.</p></div>
  <div class="mitem"><b>{{ ICON.check|safe }}Verified quotes</b><p>LLM verdicts must quote the transcript word for word. Quotes are machine-checked; anything unchecked is marked unverified, never a pass.</p></div>
  <div class="mitem"><b>{{ ICON.wave|safe }}Line vs bot</b><p>Every call is judged on what the bot really said and on what the caller heard. Noise-only failures are labelled line errors.</p></div>
  <div class="mitem"><b>{{ ICON.phone|safe }}Simulated line</b><p>Band-pass 300–3400 Hz, 8 kHz, μ-law or Opus, burst packet loss, clipping. A simulation, not a carrier network. All identifiers are fake.</p></div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
